⏭️ ColorControl StopMoveStep functionality on ExtendedColorLightEnhancedEHSXYCT (Test_TC_CC_8_1)
   ↳ The managedTransitionTimeHandling opt-in under MATTERBRIDGE_CHIP_TEST (packages/core/src/behaviors/colorControlServer.ts) fixed this test's original failure (step 9, HS Stop) and the CT/HS Stop sections that follow — the test now progresses from 10 successes/1 error to 60 successes/1 error. It still fails at step 37 (Step 5e, the EnhancedMoveHue section, second read 10s after Stop): StopMoveStep genuinely never stops an EnhancedCurrentHue transition on any Matterbridge ColorControl endpoint, because @matter/node's ColorControlServer.stopMoveStepLogic() only calls transitions.stop('enhancedCurrentHue') when 'this.state.colorLoopActive === ColorControl.ColorLoopActive.Inactive' (0) — but colorLoopActive is undefined (not 0) whenever the ColorLoop feature isn't included, which is every Matterbridge ColorControl endpoint (no createXxxColorControlClusterServer() helper enables ColorLoop), so the strict-equality guard is always false and the stop call is always skipped. Verified directly against the container with an isolated repro script: EnhancedCurrentHue keeps climbing at the full commanded rate for at least 10s after StopMoveStep is sent and acknowledged. This is a genuine @matter/node bug (an edge case the library's own guard doesn't account for), not Matterbridge code; needs a fix or workaround upstream before enabling.
